---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TeamBuilder from '../components/TeamBuilder';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pokémon Type Coverage Calculator | Super Pokémon Team Builder" description="Compare your Pokémon team's same-type offensive coverage against 18 target types and find targets you cannot hit super effectively."><SiteHeader/><main id="main"><p class="eyebrow">FIND YOUR OFFENSIVE BLIND SPOTS</p><h1>Pokémon Type Coverage Calculator</h1><p class="intro">See which single-type targets your team’s own types can hit super effectively, neutrally, or poorly.</p><TeamBuilder focus="coverage" client:load/><section class="seo-content"><h2>Coverage is about matchups</h2><p>A greater number of different team types does not automatically mean better offensive coverage. We check each team member’s own attack types against all 18 single-type targets and retain the best matchup for each target. Electric attacks cover Water and Flying, but do not affect Ground targets.</p><h3>Same-type coverage versus movesets</h3><p>The current tool assumes attacks that match a Pokémon’s own typing. Many Pokémon learn attacks of other types, and some lack useful attacks of their own type. Actual coverage requires selecting moves, which is outside this first version.</p><h3>Use both offense and defense</h3><p>Coverage contributes 25% of the planning score. Review shared weaknesses as well: a team with excellent offense can still have several members vulnerable to the same attack.</p><a href="/weakness-calculator">Review defensive weaknesses →</a></section></main><SiteFooter/></BaseLayout>
